{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789251683,"nonce":"zEpvhXU2P0EjbhzL5E7pUEp5akY=","title":"Hosted wren_lift: krio-backed fibers' stacks are unknown to the core","message":"With WLIFT_KRIO_FIBER=1 (opt-in) a wren_lift fiber runs on a krio stack\nthe core has not registered. If the thread parks at a safepoint while its\nsp is on such a stack, the core scans from that sp to the thread's stack\ntop across unmapped memory.\n\nwren_lift's seam needs fiber-stack registration slots\n(register/update_sp/unregister, as ash's has), and the adapter forwards\nthem to heap::gc_register_fiber_stack and friends. Until then the mode is\nunsupported under a host; document it.","files":null}]}